---
// CookieParserTool — reads a Cookie request header, Set-Cookie response lines (one per line,
// with or without the header name, from curl -v / -i, DevTools or Headers.get) or a Netscape
// cookies.txt file. Set-Cookie lines go through the RFC 6265bis parsing and storage rules, so
// the page says whether a browser keeps, deletes or rejects each cookie and why; a request
// simulation shows which cookies the next request carries and in what order. A builder writes
// Set-Cookie headers. Nothing is stored or sent: the page is a `disabled` sensitive tool page
// (src/data/persistence.ts), so it also loads no analytics or ad scripts.
//
// The pure functions sit between the `engine:start` / `engine:end` markers so
// scripts/test-cookie-parser.mjs runs the shipped code. TOKEN_RULES and the sensitive-name
// helpers are copied from HarFileAnalyzerTool.astro; the test checks they match.
import Toggletip from '../Toggletip.astro';

